  "crossover_analysis": "Empirical Crossover Finding: For small NFAs (|V| <= 18 states, k <= 4), the optimized Exact Analyzer is faster end-to-end than the GNN (e.g. 0.48ms for Exact vs 0.51ms for GNN at 10 states) due to PyTorch tensor creation and graph feature extraction overhead. Beyond 18 states, the GNN scales at O(|V| + |E|) while the exact product analyzer scales with product graph reachability (taking ~194ms at 122 states vs 2.5ms for GNN). Thus, the GNN does NOT possess a speed advantage on small typical regexes, but offers an empirical crossover at |V| approx 18 states.",
